    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d671">

                <pb facs="1000" n="872" xml:id="pg872"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 671.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Cox to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-10-17"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 17, 1885</date>.
                        (Received November 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 31.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    of the dispatch, with its accompanying papers, which I have sent to the Porte,
                    in protest of certain school taxes levied on the island of Mytilene.</p>
                <p>I hope it may meet with your concurrence.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>S. S. COX.</signed></closer>





